# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Same format as Netlify, so this stays
# portable if the host changes.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE — and it should stay that way.
#
# All 36 URLs the site ranks for resolve at their original paths (that is what
# `npm run build` verifies via scripts/check-parity.mjs). Nothing has moved, so
# nothing needs redirecting.
#
# Add a line here ONLY when a ranking URL genuinely has to change, and always
# as a permanent 301 so the old page's authority transfers:
#
#   /general-contractor-in-college   /general-contractor-in-fairbanks   301
#
# Never 302 a page that ranks — a temporary redirect tells Google to keep
# indexing the old URL, so you get neither page ranking properly.
#
# Cloudflare Pages caps this file at 2,000 rules and 100 dynamic (splat/
# placeholder) rules. Nowhere near either.
